<Legal
  title="Data Processing Addendum"
  description="The Article 28 terms governing iGrowFast's processing of personal data on behalf of the businesses that use it."
  path="/dpa"
  updated="16 July 2026"
  summary="For businesses using iGrowFast: the terms under which we process your customers' personal data on your instructions."
>
  <h2 id="scope">1. What this is</h2>
  <p>
    This addendum forms part of the <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>. It
    applies where you use iGrowFast to process personal data about other people
    — principally your own customers.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>You are the controller. We are the processor.</strong> You decide why
    and how your customers' data is used; we act on your instructions. For your
    own users' account data we are the controller — that is covered by the
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>, not this document.
  </p>

  <h2 id="subject">2. Subject matter, duration, nature and purpose</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th>Subject matter</th><td>Providing the iGrowFast platform to you.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Duration</th><td>For as long as your account is active, plus the deletion period in section 9.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Nature</th><td>Storage, organisation, retrieval, transmission, display, backup and deletion — carried out by the platform's normal operation.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Purpose</th><td>Order management, delivery and carrier coordination, customer messaging, advertising reporting, document generation, and reconciliation of amounts owed.</td></tr>
        <tr>
          <th>Categories of data subject</th>
          <td>Your customers; your staff; recipients of deliveries; people who message your numbers.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>Categories of personal data</th>
          <td>Names; phone numbers; delivery addresses, cities and zones; order contents and values; delivery and return status; message content and metadata (text, images, audio, documents); contact records.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>Special-category data</th>
          <td><strong>None intended.</strong> The platform is not designed for it and you should not put it in. Message content is free-form, so incidental disclosure by a customer is possible — we treat message content as sensitive in practice regardless.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="instructions">3. Our obligations</h2>
  <p>We will:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Process only on your documented instructions</strong>, including
      for transfers, unless required by law — in which case we will tell you
      first, unless the law forbids it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Tell you if an instruction appears to breach data protection
      law</strong>, rather than quietly carrying it out.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Not use your customers' data for our own purposes.</strong> We do not sell it. We do not use it to train models. We do not use it to build a product for someone else.</li>
    <li><strong>Bind everyone with access to confidentiality.</strong></li>
    <li><strong>Implement appropriate security</strong> — see section 5.</li>
    <li><strong>Help you</strong> respond to rights requests, and with your obligations on security, breach notification and impact assessments.</li>
    <li><strong>Delete or return</strong> the data at the end, per section 9.</li>
    <li><strong>Make available the information</strong> needed to show compliance, and allow audits — see section 8.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="your">4. Your obligations</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You must have a lawful basis for the data you put in.</li>
    <li>You are responsible for the accuracy of your instructions, and for your own privacy notices to your customers.</li>
    <li><strong>Consent for messaging is yours to obtain and record.</strong> See the <a href="/acceptable-use">Acceptable Use Policy</a>.</li>
    <li>You must not put special-category data into fields not designed for it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="security">5. Security</h2>
  <p>Measures in place today:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Encryption in transit for all traffic.</li>
    <li>Encryption at rest for backups.</li>
    <li>Row-level access control enforced in the database, so a user's role limits what they can retrieve — not merely what the interface shows them.</li>
    <li>Tenant isolation between businesses.</li>
    <li>Credentials and API secrets held in a dedicated secret store, not in application code.</li>
    <li>Key-based administrative access only; no password login to servers.</li>
    <li>Regular encrypted backups held in the European Union.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We assess these against the risk and update them. We are not going to claim
    they make a breach impossible.
  </p>

  <h2 id="subprocessors">6. Sub-processors</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>You give us general authorisation</strong> to engage sub-processors,
    subject to this section.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Every sub-processor is bound by written terms no less protective than these.</li>
    <li>We remain fully liable to you for their performance.</li>
    <li>
      The current list, by category, is at <a href="/sub-processors">Sub-processors</a>.
      Named detail is available to customers on request for your own compliance
      records.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Changes:</strong> we will give you reasonable advance notice before
      adding or replacing a sub-processor. You may object on reasonable data
      protection grounds. If we cannot resolve your objection, you may terminate
      the affected part of the service without penalty.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="transfers">7. International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Processing takes place in <strong>Germany</strong>; storage and backups in
    the <strong>European Union</strong>. Some data reaches the
    <strong>United States</strong>, because we are a US company.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where personal data is transferred out of the EEA, we rely on the European
    Commission's <strong>Standard Contractual Clauses</strong>, which are
    incorporated into this addendum by reference, together with a transfer impact
    assessment and supplementary measures where required.
  </p>
  <p>
    <span class="wip">In progress</span> Our transfer documentation is being
    completed, including the authorisation required under Moroccan law for
    transfers abroad, and the module selection under the Clauses is being
    confirmed with counsel. We will not tell you this is finished before it is.
  </p>

  <h2 id="audit">8. Audits and assistance</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We will answer reasonable questions about our processing in writing.</li>
    <li>On reasonable notice, not more than once a year unless a regulator requires it or there has been a breach, we will support an audit — proportionate, at your cost, and without compromising other customers' confidentiality or security.</li>
    <li>We will help you with rights requests within the limits of what the platform can do, and we will route to you anyone who contacts us directly about your data.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="deletion">9. Deletion and return</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You can export your data at any time using the features in the product.</li>
    <li>On termination, we make it available for export for a reasonable period.</li>
    <li>After that, we delete it — except where law requires retention, in which case we keep only what is required, for only as long as required.</li>
    <li>Backups: deletion propagates as backups rotate out on their schedule. They remain encrypted and access-controlled until they do.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="breach">10. Breach notification</h2>
  <p>
    If we become aware of a personal data breach affecting your data, we will
    notify you <strong>without undue delay</strong>, with what we know: what
    happened, which categories and roughly how many records, likely
    consequences, and what we are doing. We will keep you updated as we learn
    more. Notifying regulators and affected individuals is your call as the
    controller; we will give you what you need to make it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="liability">11. Liability</h2>
  <p>
    The limitations in the <a href="/terms#warranty">Terms of Service</a> apply
    to this addendum. Nothing here limits a data subject's rights, or either
    party's liability to a supervisory authority.
  </p>

  <h2 id="conflict">12. Conflict</h2>
  <p>
    Where this addendum conflicts with the Terms of Service on the processing of
    personal data, this addendum wins.
  </p>
</Legal>
